<h3><a href="/cross-reference/kr2508-jst-scn-2-5/"><span class="x-mcard__series">KR2508</span> <span class="x-mcard__eq">Equivalent to JST SCN <span class="pn">2.5</span></span></a></h3> <ul class="chips"> <li><span class="chip chip--pitch">2.50mm</span></li> <li><span class="chip">Series-level mapping</span></li> </ul> <a class="x-mcard__cta" href="/cross-reference/kr2508-jst-scn-2-5/">View mapping</a> </li><li class="x-mcard"> <h3><a href="/cross-reference/kr2516-jst-xa-2-5/"><span class="x-mcard__series">KR2516</span> <span class="x-mcard__eq">Equivalent to JST XA <span class="pn">2.5</span></span></a></h3> <ul class="chips"> <li><span class="chip chip--pitch">2.50mm</span></li> <li><span class="chip">Series-level mapping</span></li> </ul> <a class="x-mcard__cta" href="/cross-reference/kr2516-jst-xa-2-5/">View mapping</a> </li><li class="x-mcard"> <h3><a href="/cross-reference/kr2541-molex-sl-mx2-54/"><span class="x-mcard__series">KR2541</span> <span class="x-mcard__eq">Equivalent to Molex SL <span class="pn">MX2.54</span></span></a></h3> <ul class="chips"> <li><span class="chip chip--pitch">2.54mm</span></li> <li><span class="chip">Series-level mapping</span></li> </ul> <a class="x-mcard__cta" href="/cross-reference/kr2541-molex-sl-mx2-54/">View mapping</a> </li><li class="x-mcard"> <h3><a href="/cross-reference/kr3963-jst-sdn3-96/"><span class="x-mcard__series">KR3963</span> <span class="x-mcard__eq">Equivalent to JST <span class="pn">SDN3.96</span></span></a></h3> <ul class="chips"> <li><span class="chip chip--pitch">3.96mm</span></li> <li><span class="chip">Series-level mapping</span></li> </ul> <a class="x-mcard__cta" href="/cross-reference/kr3963-jst-sdn3-96/">View mapping</a> </li><li class="x-mcard"> <h3><a href="/cross-reference/kr0800-jst/"><span class="x-mcard__series">KR0800</span> <span class="x-mcard__eq">Equivalent to JST</span></a></h3> <ul class="chips">  <li><span class="chip">18 part-number rows</span></li> </ul> <a class="x-mcard__cta" href="/cross-reference/kr0800-jst/">View mapping</a> </li> </ul> </div> </section> <section class="band band--alt x-faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="x-faq-h"> <div class="container narrow"> <h2 id="x-faq-h" class="sec-title">Cross-reference FAQ</h2> <div class="x-faqs"> <div class="x-faq__item"><h3>How many part numbers does Konnra's cross-reference cover?</h3><p>Konnra's cross-list pages publish <span class="pn">840</span> incumbent part-number rows (Molex <span class="pn">552</span>, JST <span class="pn">288</span>). <span class="pn">836</span> of them list a Konnra part number and have their own page here; <span class="pn">4</span> list no Konnra part number. Konnra also publishes <span class="pn">40</span> series-level mappings across Molex, JST, Hirose, and Yeonho.</p></div><div class="x-faq__item"><h3>Which Konnra series does Konnra list against Molex <span class="pn">Mini-Fit</span> Jr <span class="pn">5556</span>, <span class="pn">5557</span>, <span class="pn">5558</span> and <span class="pn">5559</span> parts?</h3><p>Konnra lists <span class="pn">KR4200</span> (<span class="pn">4.2mm</span>) against Molex <span class="pn">Mini-Fit</span> Jr <span class="pn">5556/</span><wbr><span class="pn">5557/</span><wbr><span class="pn">5558/</span><wbr><span class="pn">5559</span> parts, with <span class="pn">108</span> part-number rows, for example <span class="pn">5557-02R2</span> → <span class="pn">H4200M1021601A</span>; <span class="pn">5557-03R2</span> → <span class="pn">H4200M1031601A</span>; <span class="pn">5557-04R2</span> → <span class="pn">H4200M1041601A</span>.</p></div><div class="x-faq__item"><h3>How should I read an entry in this cross-reference?</h3><p>Each entry is Konnra's own published statement that the Konnra part is compatible with, or an equivalent of, the incumbent part. This site reproduces Konnra's wording as published and does not add to it. Request samples to check fit in your design.</p></div> </div> </div> </section> <script>
(function () {
  var q = document.getElementById('x-q'), out = document.getElementById('x-count'), none = document.getElementById('x-none');
